WEBVTT

00:08:59.784 --> 00:09:03.150
So, we're used to not
challenging religious ideas,

00:09:03.174 --> 00:09:06.364
and it's very interesting how much
of a furor Richard creates

00:09:06.388 --> 00:09:07.547
when he does it." --

00:09:07.571 --> 00:09:09.371
He meant me, not that one.

00:09:10.578 --> 00:09:12.976
"Everybody gets absolutely
frantic about it,

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:15.588
because you're not allowed
to say these things.

00:09:15.612 --> 00:09:17.309
Yet when you look at it rationally,

00:09:17.333 --> 00:09:19.429
there's no reason why those ideas

00:09:19.453 --> 00:09:22.128
shouldn't be as open
to debate as any other,

00:09:22.152 --> 00:09:25.221
except that we've agreed
somehow between us

00:09:25.245 --> 00:09:26.619
that they shouldn't be."

00:09:26.983 --> 00:09:29.300
And that's the end
of the quote from Douglas.